is session may write only `design/` and may not read `reviews/`. So the probe was not run and no cell is scored — scoring an unread source would fabricate evidence. §9 is the hand-off (exact line forms, execution order, a format trap where `rg -c '^## goal: '` counts lines inside code fences); §10 maps each accept assertion to its design element and owner.\n\n**One accept assertion has a latent defect.** `^loss_ratio: 0\\.[0-9]+$` can express `0.00` but not exactly `1.00`. Assumption A8′ fixes the rule now rather than leaving it to be improvised under gate pressure: report the true value and let the check fail. Total loss is NO-GO regardless, and a failing gate is the correct signal — it's near-impossible in practice, since `Decision.label` and `EvidenceRef.hash` are trivially present in any review artifact.","ttft_ms":2584,"ttft_stream_ms":1132,"time_to_request_ms":78,"type":"result","duration_ms":438773,"uuid":"373629f9-9212-46f2-a4ee-30d86a5f15b3"}
